<!--
    Metadata for the dose form tests in EmrConceptServiceComponentTest, and for
    DoseFormGroupControllerTest, which exposes the same data over REST.

    Two dose form groups, each a concept set of dose forms, each mapped to a route of
    administration reference term:

      Oral Solid (5001) -> Tablet (5011), Capsule (5012)
        route term ROUTE-ORAL (5031), which concept Oral (5021) claims via a SAME-AS mapping
        route term ROUTE-RETIRED (5033), which only the retired concept Retired Oral (5022)
        claims via SAME-AS
      Injectable (5002) -> Solution for Injection (5013)
        route term ROUTE-UNRESOLVED (5032), which no concept claims via SAME-AS

    Ointment (5014) is a dose form belonging to no group at all, which is allowed: it is still
    returned, with an empty list of dose form groups.

    Retired Tablet (5015), Retired Group (5004) and Retired Oral (5022) are retired and so must not
    be returned at all, not even as a group of Tablet, which Retired Group claims.
    ConceptService.getConceptsByClass() does not filter on retired, so EmrConceptService has to.

    Retired Group is also mapped to route term ROUTE-RECTAL (5035), which the non-retired concept
    Rectal (5024) claims via SAME-AS. That route resolves perfectly well and is reachable from
    Tablet, so the only thing keeping it out of getRoutesOfAdministration(Tablet) is the retired
    check on the parent sets: ConceptService.getSetsContainingConcept() does not filter on retired
    either.

    Note that term 5031 carries mappings of two different types (route-of-administration from
    the group, SAME-AS from the route concept). That is deliberate: it is the case
    ConceptService.getConceptByMapping() rejects, and the reason routes are resolved with
    EmrConceptService.getConceptsSameAs() instead.

    The "same-as" concept map type (id 2) and the "Misc" (11) concept class come from the core
    standardTestDataset; the route-of-administration map type and the "Drug form" and "Dose Form
    Group" concept classes do not, so they are created here. The dose form concept class really is
    named "Drug form" in the dictionary, which is why that name is used here.
-->
